#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'EOF'
Skald macOS release validation checklist

Automated checks:
- Build a Developer ID package from the release tag with just macos-package.
- Submit it with just macos-notarize.
- Run SKALD_REQUIRE_DEVELOPER_ID=1 just macos-release-check.
- Confirm the release contains only the allowlisted app files, DMG, and checksum.

Clean install on an Apple Silicon macOS 14+ account:
- Verify the downloaded DMG checksum, open it, and drag Skald to Applications.
- Open Skald without bypassing Gatekeeper.
- Install the daemon and install/select small.en-q5 from the embedded CLI.
- Grant Microphone and Accessibility access through normal macOS prompts.
- Confirm doctor reports the daemon, model, broker, target, clipboard, and paste readiness.
- Dictate into TextEdit with the global shortcut and confirm automatic paste.
- Dictate in Terminal and confirm clipboard-only output followed by manual Command-V.
- Log out and back in; confirm the LaunchAgent and menu app recover normally.

Upgrade from the previous release:
- Back up config.toml, install the new app over the old app, and reopen it.
- Run config upgrade and Install or repair daemon from the new app.
- Confirm models, settings, styles, snippets, and Keychain access remain available.
- Repeat doctor, TextEdit dictation, and Terminal clipboard validation.

Rollback:
- Quit Skald, install the previous app, and restore its saved config if needed.
- Run Install or repair daemon from the restored app.
- Repeat doctor and the full dictation path.

Uninstall:
- Run service uninstall from the embedded CLI, quit Skald, and remove the app.
- Confirm the LaunchAgent is absent. Remove retained data and the OpenRouter
  Keychain secret only when testing a complete data purge.

Record the macOS version, hardware, release tag, signing identity, notary
submission ID, and any failed item in the release notes.
EOF

